02:11:22.388 advertise: AUTO - each client is told the host it can actually reach:
02:11:22.388   a client on a private, loopback, link-local or CGNAT address is told the
02:11:22.388   address it reached this server on; a client on a public address is told
02:11:22.389   this box's public address, below.
02:11:22.389   public address: 108.20.162.119 (from checkip.amazonaws.com, re-checked every 10 min)
02:11:22.389   channel 0: port 8485, host decided per connection
02:11:22.389   channel 1: port 8486, host decided per connection
02:11:22.389 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
02:11:22.389   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
02:11:22.389 SET-FIELD PROBE IS ON - which by now means 'the channel answers at all'. The
02:11:22.389   flag is a misnomer kept for the launch line: without it Session::handle
02:11:22.389   returns nothing for every packet, so the migration hello goes unanswered and
02:11:22.389   the client freezes on 'Connecting...'.
02:11:22.389   With it on, this channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
02:11:22.389   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
02:11:22.389   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
02:11:22.389   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
02:11:22.389   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
02:11:22.389   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
02:11:22.389   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
02:11:22.389   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
02:11:22.389   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
